### Component 2: Cross-Modal Bridge - Manifold-Constrained Hyper-Connections

Implement mHC architecture for text-to-image conditioning in Zig:

**mHC Mathematical Specification:**
- Hyper-connection matrix Hᵣₑₛ: n×n doubly stochastic matrix where n=4 (number of lanes)
- Birkhoff polytope projection using Sinkhorn-Knopp algorithm: iterative row/column normalization
- Propagation formula: x_{l+1} = Hᵣₑₛ · [lane₁, lane₂, lane₃, lane₄]ᵀ
- Identity mapping restoration: Hᵣₑₛ must satisfy ∑ᵢ Hᵢⱼ = 1, ∑ⱼ Hᵢⱼ = 1
- Gradient amplification constraint: maintain gradient norm ratio < 1.6 (vs 3000 in standard residual)

**Four-Lane Semantic Architecture:**
